WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.110
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.380 --> 01:34.920
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.250 --> 01:37.650
[Episode 45]

4
01:43.130 --> 01:43.970
Jianying!

5
01:45.360 --> 01:46.759
Did everyone make it out?

6
01:46.880 --> 01:48.080
Yes, they all made it.

7
01:48.080 --> 01:49.080
Xiangrong,

8
01:49.440 --> 01:51.720
this is our only map of Gansu.

9
01:52.130 --> 01:56.270
[Xiao Xiangrong, Secretary-General of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

10
01:52.450 --> 01:53.440
You must keep it safe

11
01:53.440 --> 01:55.720
and hand it over to the Military Commission chief.

12
01:55.720 --> 01:56.850
Rest assured.

13
02:13.050 --> 02:14.410
Go. Let's go.

14
02:21.120 --> 02:22.720
Careful with the equipment!

15
02:25.640 --> 02:26.570
Watch your step.

16
02:32.930 --> 02:33.760
Shangkun.

17
02:34.400 --> 02:34.840
Jianying.

18
02:34.840 --> 02:35.640
Has everyone evacuated?

19
02:35.640 --> 02:36.840
Yes, everyone's out,

20
02:36.960 --> 02:39.329
except for Bo Zhao and a few comrades from the propaganda troupe,

21
02:39.329 --> 02:41.050
who went to the 4th Red Army for a performance.

22
02:41.050 --> 02:42.210
We can't reach them right now,

23
02:42.210 --> 02:43.210
so there's no way to notify them.

24
02:43.130 --> 02:46.150
[Yang Shangkun, Deputy Director of the Red Army General Political Department]

25
02:44.170 --> 02:45.500
After we part this time,

26
02:45.800 --> 02:48.200
I wonder if we'll ever see each other again.

27
02:52.870 --> 02:55.790
[Ye Jianying, Chief of Staff of Red Army Frontline General Headquarters]

28
02:54.550 --> 02:56.290
We must have faith in the Central Committee.

29
02:56.290 --> 02:58.090
You will definitely meet again.

30
02:58.730 --> 02:59.730
Let's get moving.

31
03:15.490 --> 03:16.380
Zedong,

32
03:18.079 --> 03:19.560
I've thought it over.

33
03:20.120 --> 03:22.329
We should send Xu and Chen

34
03:22.329 --> 03:23.400
a telegram

35
03:23.400 --> 03:25.800
to explain our reasons for marching north.

36
03:26.240 --> 03:28.640
Let's make one last effort to win them over.

37
03:28.930 --> 03:29.770
Agreed.

38
03:30.360 --> 03:32.160
We do everything out in the open.

39
03:33.500 --> 03:34.660
You guys go on ahead.

40
03:34.690 --> 03:36.290
I'll wait here for Jianying.

41
03:41.320 --> 03:42.490
Xiao, put me down.

42
03:51.210 --> 03:51.930
Chairman Mao!

43
03:51.930 --> 03:52.770
Jianying!

44
03:53.120 --> 03:54.520
We brought out the Central directly affiliated units.

45
03:54.520 --> 03:55.450
All out?

46
03:55.770 --> 03:56.560
Excellent.

47
03:57.350 --> 03:58.560
We set out six hours ago.

48
03:58.560 --> 03:59.890
How far have we marched?

49
04:00.490 --> 04:01.610
Less than 30 li.

50
04:04.520 --> 04:06.550
The comrades from the Central Committee need to pick up the pace,

51
04:06.550 --> 04:07.580
just in case.

52
04:08.290 --> 04:08.690
Luofu,

53
04:09.250 --> 04:10.180
here's the plan.

54
04:10.350 --> 04:12.050
You lead the directly affiliated units ahead,

55
04:12.050 --> 04:12.760
and I'll bring up the rear.

56
04:12.760 --> 04:13.640
Zedong,

57
04:14.010 --> 04:15.210
you can't stay in the rear.

58
04:15.210 --> 04:16.540
It's far too dangerous.

59
04:16.560 --> 04:17.970
It's actually better if I stay behind.

60
04:17.970 --> 04:19.149
If they catch up to us,

61
04:19.149 --> 04:20.660
with me here as the Chairman of the Soviet,

62
04:20.660 --> 04:22.010
I can still try to reason with them.

63
04:22.010 --> 04:23.130
Absolutely not.

64
04:24.050 --> 04:26.000
You're a thorn in Zhang Guotao's side right now.

65
04:26.000 --> 04:28.030
If anything happens to you, how could we answer for it?

66
04:28.030 --> 04:29.680
I'm a thorn in Chiang Kai-shek's side too.

67
04:29.680 --> 04:31.390
If none of us can get away, there'll be nothing to answer for.

68
04:31.390 --> 04:33.040
Being a thorn in the side has its perks.

69
04:33.040 --> 04:35.050
With me here, they'll have something to show for it.

70
04:35.050 --> 04:36.530
Better than none of us getting away, so hurry up!

71
04:36.530 --> 04:38.070
Zedong, you...

72
04:42.800 --> 04:45.320
Please don't worry, commanders.

73
04:45.350 --> 04:46.620
I'll stick with Mao.

74
04:52.990 --> 04:53.650
Let's go.

75
04:55.340 --> 04:55.810
Move out.

76
04:55.810 --> 04:56.230
Here.

77
04:57.320 --> 04:57.860
Lift!

78
05:04.760 --> 05:05.440
Report!

79
05:06.050 --> 05:06.680
Political Commissar!

80
05:06.680 --> 05:07.490
Commander-in-Chief!

81
05:07.490 --> 05:08.150
Chief of Staff Ye

82
05:08.150 --> 05:11.750
took the Central directly affiliated units and left overnight.

83
05:12.130 --> 05:13.660
Weren't they just out foraging for grain?

84
05:13.660 --> 05:15.320
They took all the weapons, gear, and equipment

85
05:15.320 --> 05:15.970
with them.

86
05:16.050 --> 05:16.760
They even took the map of Gansu Province

87
05:16.760 --> 05:18.380
from the headquarters!

88
05:27.360 --> 05:28.120
What?

89
05:28.530 --> 05:30.790
Alright, I'll report this immediately.

90
05:31.490 --> 05:33.930
Commissar, it's not just the directly affiliated units!

91
05:33.930 --> 05:35.380
The 3rd Red Army Corps has also moved out.

92
05:35.380 --> 05:36.880
Commissar, the 4th Red Army reports

93
05:36.880 --> 05:38.490
that the 1st Front Army is marching north.

94
05:38.490 --> 05:40.850
Commissar, was there an emergency order?

95
05:40.710 --> 05:43.140
[He Wei, Political Commissar of the Red Army University]

96
05:40.920 --> 05:43.490
Everyone from the Red Army University cleared out overnight!

97
05:43.490 --> 05:46.060
Hello, this is the General Frontline Command.

98
05:46.060 --> 05:46.990
What did you say?

99
05:47.560 --> 05:48.270
Hold on.

100
05:48.710 --> 05:51.840
Commissar, the troops are asking if they should attack.

101
05:51.850 --> 05:53.450
[Li Te, Deputy Chief of Staff of the 4th Front Army and Dean of Education of the Red Army University]

102
05:55.370 --> 05:56.659
Hello? Hello?

103
05:57.090 --> 06:00.000
Commissar, do we fire or not?

104
06:01.050 --> 06:02.880
Commissar? Hello?

105
06:03.730 --> 06:05.200
Commissar, they're leaving.

106
06:05.200 --> 06:06.800
I'm waiting for your orders.

107
06:07.440 --> 06:08.090
Hello?

108
06:08.090 --> 06:08.930
Xiangqian!

109
06:10.260 --> 06:11.610
Xiangqian, say something!

110
06:11.610 --> 06:12.490
Do we fire?

111
06:13.090 --> 06:13.950
Commissar!

112
06:14.170 --> 06:15.700
Commissar, can you hear me?

113
06:16.480 --> 06:18.510
I'm waiting for your orders. They're leaving!

114
06:18.510 --> 06:20.020
Do we fire or not?

115
06:20.760 --> 06:23.820
There is no reason for the Red Army to fight the Red Army.

116
06:27.120 --> 06:28.440
Order all troops

117
06:28.760 --> 06:30.050
to obey commands.

118
06:30.200 --> 06:32.340
Under no circumstances are we to fire.

119
06:34.610 --> 06:36.560
Do not fire. Wait for orders.

120
06:36.880 --> 06:39.880
Report! Urgent telegram from the Central Committee.

121
06:41.880 --> 06:42.760
To Xu and Chen:

122
06:42.970 --> 06:44.930
First, the current strategic policy's

123
06:44.930 --> 06:46.610
only correct decision

124
06:46.850 --> 06:48.159
is to advance rapidly north.

125
06:48.159 --> 06:49.940
The multifaceted reasons for this

126
06:49.940 --> 06:52.560
have been detailed in previous decisions and telegrams.

127
06:52.560 --> 06:53.170
Second,

128
06:53.320 --> 06:56.040
the telegram from Zhu and Zhang on the 8th ordering you south

129
06:56.040 --> 06:59.480
clearly violates the Central Committee's repeated decisions and telegrams.

130
06:59.480 --> 07:03.000
The Central Committee has wired Zhu and Zhang to cancel that order.

131
07:03.000 --> 07:03.610
Third,

132
07:03.800 --> 07:05.450
to lose no time in realizing

133
07:05.470 --> 07:07.030
our own strategic plan,

134
07:07.060 --> 07:09.170
the Central Committee has ordered the 1st Front Army's main force

135
07:09.170 --> 07:11.200
to advance toward Luoda and Lajie.

136
07:11.700 --> 07:14.160
Fourth, the 30th Army is under your command,

137
07:14.240 --> 07:17.240
and should advance following the 1st and 3rd Armies within days,

138
07:17.240 --> 07:19.440
tasked with supporting the 1st and 3rd Armies.

139
07:19.440 --> 07:22.090
Henceforth, the Right Route Army is unified under the command of

140
07:22.090 --> 07:23.410
CMC Vice Chairman Comrade Zhou Enlai.

141
07:23.410 --> 07:25.980
Fourth, as General Political Commissar Zhang

142
07:25.980 --> 07:28.030
has failed to fulfill his duties

143
07:28.410 --> 07:30.240
and has defied the Central Committee's strategic policy,

144
07:30.240 --> 07:32.610
the Central Committee hereby orders the frontline commanders

145
07:32.610 --> 07:35.930
and political commissars

146
07:36.050 --> 07:37.580
to implement its decision.

147
07:37.880 --> 07:41.680
Issued by the Central Politburo at Axi on September 10.

148
07:47.730 --> 07:48.930
Since it's like this,

149
07:49.530 --> 07:50.970
then we part ways.

150
07:52.120 --> 07:53.170
They go their way,

151
07:53.560 --> 07:56.360
and we go ours.

152
07:56.440 --> 07:57.200
No.

153
07:57.320 --> 07:58.650
It's fine for them to go,

154
07:58.680 --> 07:59.760
but there are people from our 4th Front Army

155
07:59.760 --> 08:01.290
at the Red Army University.

156
08:01.360 --> 08:02.730
We can't let them take away our men!

157
08:02.730 --> 08:03.760
I will immediately lead a team

158
08:03.760 --> 08:05.320
to get our cadets back.

159
08:05.350 --> 08:06.310
Wait a minute.

160
08:07.650 --> 08:09.530
I will write a letter to Peng Dehuai.

161
08:09.530 --> 08:10.530
You hand it to him.

162
08:54.910 --> 08:55.790
Mao,

163
08:56.370 --> 08:58.380
I've sent a telegram to Lin Biao and Nie Rongzhen,

164
08:58.380 --> 08:58.930
informing them

165
08:58.930 --> 09:01.370
that the Central Committee and the 3rd Red Army have headed north,

166
09:01.370 --> 09:03.970
and telling them to prepare food and quarters.

167
09:04.370 --> 09:05.200
Good.

168
09:07.010 --> 09:09.680
Peng, you've been working hard all night.

169
09:09.800 --> 09:11.440
Lean back and rest for a bit.

170
09:18.830 --> 09:21.360
How happy we were when we first joined forces!

171
09:22.050 --> 09:23.720
Our morale was so high.

172
09:24.680 --> 09:25.930
Over two months

173
09:27.250 --> 09:28.680
and now it's come to this.

174
09:29.080 --> 09:31.540
Zhang Guotao has done

175
09:31.650 --> 09:35.510
what Chiang Kai-shek's hundreds of thousands of troops failed to do.

176
09:37.170 --> 09:38.050
Mao,

177
09:38.690 --> 09:42.050
the Central Committee handled this incident very well.

178
09:42.360 --> 09:45.640
You deserve a lot of credit.

179
09:45.940 --> 09:48.890
Your role was crucial.

180
09:47.130 --> 09:48.790
[Li De, Comintern Military Advisor, Red Army University Instructor]

181
09:50.960 --> 09:53.210
Thank you, Comrade Li De.

182
09:54.050 --> 09:56.320
Chairman Mao, did you understand him?

183
09:56.410 --> 09:57.440
Not a word.

184
09:58.720 --> 10:00.770
But he must be praising me.

185
10:02.050 --> 10:02.930
Indeed.

186
10:04.200 --> 10:05.170
Shangkun,

187
10:05.520 --> 10:07.820
what did this foreign advisor praise the Chairman for?

188
10:07.820 --> 10:09.220
Translate for everyone.

189
10:09.330 --> 10:10.140
Sure.

190
10:11.530 --> 10:12.770
Comrade Li De said,

191
10:12.930 --> 10:14.960
the Central Committee handled this incident

192
10:14.960 --> 10:16.320
extremely well,

193
10:16.480 --> 10:18.250
and Comrade Mao Zedong deserves a lot of credit

194
10:18.250 --> 10:19.580
and was very important!

195
10:20.530 --> 10:23.390
This foreign advisor knows how to speak fairly now.

196
10:24.290 --> 10:25.130
Li De,

197
10:25.350 --> 10:26.530
do you know the saying,

198
10:26.530 --> 10:29.460
"A wastrel feels no pain selling his father's land"?

199
10:31.320 --> 10:32.400
What did he say?

200
10:32.800 --> 10:33.930
Translate it for me.

201
10:35.080 --> 10:35.720
Comrade...

202
10:35.720 --> 10:37.050
The 4th Front Army!

203
10:52.930 --> 10:54.800
Chairman, it's Li Te and his men! They've caught up!

204
10:54.800 --> 10:55.560
Protect Chairman Mao!

205
10:55.560 --> 10:56.200
Yes, sir!

206
10:56.250 --> 10:57.850
10th Regiment, come with me!

207
10:59.850 --> 11:02.200
Don't head north with those opportunists!

208
11:02.200 --> 11:04.200
Follow me south, and let's eat rice!

209
11:04.410 --> 11:05.200
Li Te!

210
11:06.600 --> 11:08.330
What do you think you're doing?

211
11:16.660 --> 11:19.260
I'm under orders from Commissar Chen Changhao

212
11:19.770 --> 11:21.890
to bring the 4th Front Army cadets back.

213
11:21.890 --> 11:23.600
The Red Army University is marching north

214
11:23.600 --> 11:25.010
on direct orders from the Central Committee.

215
11:25.010 --> 11:26.410
Does your Commissar Chen

216
11:27.130 --> 11:29.460
think he commands the Central Committee?

217
11:37.890 --> 11:39.680
Here is a letter from Commissar Chen.

218
11:39.680 --> 11:40.600
He says

219
11:40.890 --> 11:43.010
he hopes you'll listen to Chairman Zhang

220
11:43.010 --> 11:44.480
and head south with us.

221
11:44.950 --> 11:48.100
I answer only to the Central Committee!

222
11:50.680 --> 11:52.250
I'll write you a receipt.

223
12:02.650 --> 12:05.310
[For Comrade Peng Dehuai. Until we meet again.]

224
12:07.770 --> 12:08.540
You!

225
12:13.020 --> 12:15.490
Cadets of the 4th Front Army, fall in!

226
12:15.600 --> 12:17.170
We're heading back right now.

227
12:17.170 --> 12:19.330
Defy me at your own peril.

228
12:28.850 --> 12:30.260
What are you staring at?

229
12:30.600 --> 12:32.080
Are you refusing Chairman Zhang's orders?

230
12:32.080 --> 12:34.080
This is pure insubordination!

231
12:34.240 --> 12:35.120
Li Te!

232
12:36.920 --> 12:40.430
The Central Committee has every right to dictate its own strategy!

233
12:40.430 --> 12:43.190
Who are you to stand in their way?

234
12:43.440 --> 12:44.600
You were sent here by the Comintern,

235
12:44.600 --> 12:45.870
but this stunt you're pulling

236
12:45.870 --> 12:47.590
hasn't been authorized by them at all.

237
12:47.590 --> 12:49.020
It's completely wrong!

238
12:49.050 --> 12:50.600
You're the one who's wrong!

239
12:50.930 --> 12:54.720
The Politburo alone decides our strategy!

240
12:54.890 --> 12:55.930
Your violent interference

241
12:55.930 --> 12:57.480
is just like Zhang Guotao's,

242
12:57.480 --> 12:59.200
wrong and utterly stupid!

243
12:59.200 --> 13:01.200
You red imperialist!

244
13:01.530 --> 13:02.990
You're acting like a thug!

245
13:05.170 --> 13:07.680
Li De just called Li Te a thug,

246
13:07.980 --> 13:10.310
and Li Te called him a red imperialist.

247
13:11.210 --> 13:14.490
Let me tell you something, Li Te. As long as I'm standing here,

248
13:14.490 --> 13:16.570
you aren't taking a single man with you!

249
13:16.570 --> 13:18.070
The Red Army is marching north,

250
13:18.070 --> 13:19.890
executing the orders of the Central Committee.

251
13:19.890 --> 13:21.250
If you dare to defy them,

252
13:21.320 --> 13:23.250
you're a counter-revolutionary!

253
13:23.720 --> 13:25.300
And I will have you shot!

254
13:40.840 --> 13:41.880
No!

255
13:46.200 --> 13:47.560
Stand down, all of you!

256
13:47.890 --> 13:48.680
Chairman.

257
13:49.590 --> 13:51.850
Are we really going to fire on our own men?

258
13:58.440 --> 13:59.320
Mao Zedong!

259
13:59.560 --> 14:00.290
You're nothing but a

260
14:00.290 --> 14:02.270
cowardly opportunist running for his life!

261
14:02.270 --> 14:04.630
Comrade Li Te, let me ask you something.

262
14:05.130 --> 14:08.680
We broke through layer after layer of Nationalist blockades

263
14:08.720 --> 14:09.830
to march north and fight Japan.

264
14:09.830 --> 14:11.950
Is that cowardly opportunism?

265
14:11.970 --> 14:15.430
Or is it your Chairman Zhang, fleeing south to dodge the fight,

266
14:16.000 --> 14:18.130
who is the real cowardly opportunist?

267
14:18.160 --> 14:21.490
Our Chairman Zhang is the General Commissar of the Red Army!

268
14:21.770 --> 14:23.370
His orders are to head south!

269
14:23.440 --> 14:24.200
You people

270
14:24.310 --> 14:26.570
are committing total insubordination!

271
14:27.480 --> 14:28.560
Marching north

272
14:28.930 --> 14:31.090
is a resolution passed by the Politburo.

273
14:31.090 --> 14:33.220
Tell me, since when does the Politburo

274
14:33.320 --> 14:35.600
need to ask Commissar Zhang for permission?

275
14:35.600 --> 14:37.080
I don't care where the rest of you go,

276
14:37.080 --> 14:38.890
but these cadets of the 4th Front Army

277
14:38.890 --> 14:40.550
are coming back with me today!

278
14:59.530 --> 15:02.610
Comrades, we are the Red Army.

279
15:03.600 --> 15:06.330
We are an army led by the Communist Party of China.

280
15:06.890 --> 15:08.140
We are a family!

281
15:09.130 --> 15:12.740
Now, someone is hell-bent on tearing this family apart.

282
15:13.800 --> 15:16.160
Your commander demands you return.

283
15:16.960 --> 15:18.070
If you wish to go,

284
15:19.370 --> 15:20.420
then go.

285
15:21.650 --> 15:25.550
But please take the Central Committee's

286
15:25.940 --> 15:29.540
"Message to Comrades on the Northern Advance" with you.

287
15:30.410 --> 15:31.410
When you get back,

288
15:31.840 --> 15:34.440
please pass a message to Comrade Zhang Guotao.

289
15:34.440 --> 15:37.200
Tell him there is no future in heading south.

290
15:37.930 --> 15:39.960
I firmly believe that within a year,

291
15:40.530 --> 15:42.060
you will all come back to us.

292
15:42.310 --> 15:44.430
And no matter when you return,

293
15:46.250 --> 15:48.180
we will welcome you with open arms.

294
16:06.320 --> 16:07.170
4th Army!

295
16:07.550 --> 16:08.320
Let's go!

296
16:11.840 --> 16:12.770
Move!

297
16:14.290 --> 16:14.980
Hurry up!

298
16:18.570 --> 16:19.430
Did you hear me?

299
16:19.450 --> 16:20.290
4th Army!

300
16:20.440 --> 16:21.130
Let's move!

301
16:24.890 --> 16:25.800
Hurry!

302
16:27.260 --> 16:28.190
Hurry up!

303
17:28.990 --> 17:31.510
Comrade Li De, you've changed.

304
17:32.070 --> 17:34.860
You used to wear boots,

305
17:35.080 --> 17:37.600
but now you're in straw sandals.

306
17:48.810 --> 17:49.920
Fall in!

307
17:50.800 --> 17:52.170
Left face!

308
17:53.370 --> 17:54.040
Forward march!

309
17:54.040 --> 17:55.410
Attention, everyone!

310
17:55.410 --> 17:56.440
Forward march!

311
17:58.090 --> 17:59.130
Forward march!

312
18:12.040 --> 18:14.520
Many years later, in 1960,

313
18:15.130 --> 18:16.960
Mao Zedong met with the American writer

314
18:16.960 --> 18:18.330
Edgar Snow.

315
18:18.810 --> 18:19.760
When asked

316
18:19.760 --> 18:21.720
about the darkest moment

317
18:21.720 --> 18:22.960
of his life,

318
18:23.610 --> 18:24.810
Mao replied

319
18:25.570 --> 18:28.520
that it was during the Long March in 1935,

320
18:28.650 --> 18:31.890
amidst the struggle with Zhang Guotao in the grasslands.

321
18:33.510 --> 18:34.890
The snow-capped mountains and the treacherous grasslands

322
18:34.890 --> 18:37.550
couldn't stop the Red Army from joining forces.

323
18:38.040 --> 18:39.970
Chiang Kai-shek's relentless pursuit and blockade

324
18:39.970 --> 18:42.820
couldn't stop the Red Army from marching north.

325
18:43.370 --> 18:45.960
But because of Zhang Guotao's separatist actions,

326
18:45.960 --> 18:49.090
the Party and the Red Army went through

327
18:49.200 --> 18:51.570
the most thrilling, the longest,

328
18:51.720 --> 18:54.890
and the most perilous journey since the Long March began.

329
18:54.890 --> 18:57.890
At that time, Zhang Guotao took away 80,000 Red Army soldiers,

330
18:57.890 --> 19:00.480
including those assigned to the Left Route Army—

331
19:00.480 --> 19:02.680
the 5th Army of the original 1st Front Red Army

332
19:02.680 --> 19:04.610
and the 32nd Army (formerly the 9th Red Army Corps).

333
19:04.610 --> 19:06.280
Meanwhile, those who followed the Party Central Committee north—

334
19:06.280 --> 19:08.140
the 1st and 3rd Armies—

335
19:08.160 --> 19:10.770
amounted to less than 10,000 men.

336
19:11.680 --> 19:13.650
Facing an uncertain future,

337
19:13.960 --> 19:15.770
every member of the Communist Party

338
19:15.770 --> 19:17.570
and every soldier of the Red Army

339
19:17.570 --> 19:20.040
plunged into profound agony.

340
19:20.610 --> 19:23.470
And the only thing that kept them going until the end

341
19:23.490 --> 19:25.290
was their loyalty to the Party.

342
19:26.060 --> 19:28.760
Firmly upholding the leadership of the Central Committee

343
19:28.760 --> 19:30.810
and steadfastly following its lead

344
19:31.130 --> 19:33.240
was the beacon of light

345
19:33.610 --> 19:35.330
that every member of the Communist Party

346
19:35.330 --> 19:37.080
and every soldier of the Red Army

347
19:37.080 --> 19:40.030
ignited in their hearts during that dark period.

348
19:48.170 --> 19:49.700
Comrades, what's all this?

349
19:50.000 --> 19:51.000
Yujie (Zhu De).

350
19:52.610 --> 19:53.570
Comrade Guotao!

351
19:53.720 --> 19:55.520
I've brought you some supplies.

352
19:56.240 --> 19:57.250
I brought you some

353
19:57.270 --> 19:58.780
firewood and butter.

354
19:59.300 --> 20:00.460
This place

355
20:00.480 --> 20:02.200
gets freezing and unbearable at night.

356
20:02.200 --> 20:03.930
You'll definitely need these.

357
20:04.040 --> 20:04.970
Comrade Guotao,

358
20:05.410 --> 20:07.040
that's very thoughtful of you,

359
20:07.040 --> 20:08.570
but we have everything we need here.

360
20:08.570 --> 20:10.170
You'd better take this stuff

361
20:10.240 --> 20:12.040
to where it's needed most.

362
20:12.280 --> 20:13.680
Comrade Keqing is a woman.

363
20:13.680 --> 20:16.340
You might tough it out, but she certainly can't.

364
20:16.620 --> 20:17.500
Comrade Guotao,

365
20:17.500 --> 20:18.280
the commander and I

366
20:18.280 --> 20:19.810
are doing just fine living here.

367
20:19.810 --> 20:20.850
Thank you,

368
20:20.850 --> 20:22.420
but we really don't lack anything.

369
20:22.420 --> 20:23.820
[Kang Keqing, Zhu De's wife]

370
20:28.930 --> 20:31.720
Don't you think this room is cramped enough?

371
20:31.890 --> 20:33.690
Get out and catch some fresh air.

372
20:41.000 --> 20:42.130
I'll leave you to it.

373
20:44.670 --> 20:45.600
Comrade Guotao,

374
20:45.680 --> 20:46.810
please have a seat.

375
20:46.840 --> 20:48.640
No, no, you stay seated.

376
20:48.960 --> 20:50.020
I'll just sit here.

377
20:53.370 --> 20:54.200
Yujie,

378
20:55.480 --> 20:56.810
take a look at this.

379
20:59.200 --> 21:00.200
Mao Zedong

380
21:00.410 --> 21:02.650
took the Central Committee and the 1st and 3rd Armies

381
21:02.650 --> 21:03.580
and walked away.

382
21:04.330 --> 21:06.040
Isn't that incredibly irresponsible?

383
21:06.040 --> 21:08.370
He's treating the revolution like a joke!

384
21:09.410 --> 21:11.500
Are there some underlying reasons?

385
21:13.240 --> 21:14.720
As for the reasons,

386
21:15.760 --> 21:17.820
you should know them better than I do.

387
21:18.200 --> 21:19.570
Lately,

388
21:20.040 --> 21:21.840
our communication with the Central Committee

389
21:21.840 --> 21:24.350
has been in both our names.

390
21:25.610 --> 21:28.680
Yet there are many things I'm completely in the dark about.

391
21:28.680 --> 21:30.330
But one thing I know for sure:

392
21:30.570 --> 21:33.280
you ordering Chen Changhao and Xu Xiangqian to march south

393
21:33.280 --> 21:35.570
is something the Central Committee would never agree to.

394
21:35.570 --> 21:39.430
The Central Committee doesn't want to see a split within the Red Army.

395
21:39.520 --> 21:42.100
Since they couldn't command you,

396
21:42.520 --> 21:44.850
they had no choice but to head north first.

397
21:46.410 --> 21:47.520
But no matter how you spin it,

398
21:47.520 --> 21:48.330
at this point,

399
21:48.410 --> 21:51.010
it's the Central Committee that abandoned us.

400
21:51.440 --> 21:53.760
What kind of position does that put us in?

401
21:55.570 --> 21:57.370
What's the Red Army's next move?

402
21:58.650 --> 22:01.190
I think it's time you took a stand.

403
22:10.840 --> 22:12.760
Fine, Comrade Guotao.

404
22:13.000 --> 22:15.000
I can make my stance clear right now.

405
22:18.520 --> 22:19.960
The Central Committee is still here.

406
22:19.960 --> 22:23.630
In our Red Army, the Party commands the gun,

407
22:24.000 --> 22:27.060
and the officers must answer to the Central Committee.

408
22:51.370 --> 22:52.170
Fortunately,

409
22:52.650 --> 22:55.040
they took less than 10,000 men with them.

410
22:55.480 --> 22:57.880
The bulk of the Red Army is still on our side.

411
22:58.000 --> 22:59.130
Yujie,

412
22:59.970 --> 23:02.090
you and I are both leaders of the Red Army.

413
23:02.090 --> 23:04.820
We must stay united at a critical time like this.

414
23:05.650 --> 23:08.180
A family cannot walk down two separate paths.

415
23:08.650 --> 23:09.570
You're right.

416
23:10.280 --> 23:13.130
A family cannot walk down two separate paths.

417
23:19.960 --> 23:22.890
Alright, I'll take my leave.

418
23:28.570 --> 23:29.760
Comrade Keqing,

419
23:29.850 --> 23:32.980
I've long heard you're the Red Army's female commander,

420
23:33.240 --> 23:34.770
and an absolute crack shot,

421
23:34.890 --> 23:37.520
but you ought to know your way around a kitchen too!

422
23:37.520 --> 23:39.520
I've been sitting here all this time,

423
23:39.520 --> 23:42.320
and I haven't even been offered a cup of butter tea.

424
23:57.810 --> 23:58.960
What should we do?

425
23:59.760 --> 24:01.280
Stand with the Central Committee

426
24:01.280 --> 24:02.340
without wavering.

427
24:02.720 --> 24:05.320
But we can't fall out with Zhang Guotao either.

428
24:06.440 --> 24:07.440
It's a tough spot.

429
24:17.090 --> 24:17.850
Keqing,

430
24:18.650 --> 24:20.410
it's too risky for me to go out right now.

431
24:20.410 --> 24:21.610
Go and fetch Bocheng.

432
24:21.760 --> 24:22.620
What about you?

433
24:22.710 --> 24:23.630
Didn't you see his

434
24:23.630 --> 24:24.870
weird attitude?

435
24:24.890 --> 24:27.220
Who knows what tricks he has up his sleeve.

436
24:27.520 --> 24:28.720
Don't worry about me.

437
24:29.330 --> 24:32.570
I'm the Commander-in-Chief of the Red Army.

438
24:32.720 --> 24:34.410
Whether Zhang Guotao acknowledges it or not,

439
24:34.410 --> 24:35.370
for most of the comrades

440
24:35.370 --> 24:38.040
in the 4th Front Army,

441
24:38.170 --> 24:39.930
my words still carry some weight.

442
24:39.930 --> 24:40.720
I believe

443
24:40.870 --> 24:43.000
not everyone is going to take his side.

444
24:43.480 --> 24:45.200
We have to do everything in our power

445
24:45.200 --> 24:46.440
to unite the rank-and-file.

446
24:46.440 --> 24:47.280
Alright.

447
24:48.960 --> 24:49.730
Wait.

448
25:08.360 --> 25:10.990
[E'jie, Gansu]

449
25:08.440 --> 25:10.810
On September 12, 1935,

450
25:10.930 --> 25:13.130
the CPC Central Committee held an enlarged Politburo meeting

451
25:13.130 --> 25:15.200
in E'jie, Gansu.

452
25:15.460 --> 25:17.790
Mao Zedong delivered the meeting report.

453
25:21.570 --> 25:22.480
Comrades,

454
25:24.330 --> 25:26.680
this is exactly how the dispute

455
25:26.960 --> 25:28.370
between the Party Central Committee and Zhang Guotao,

456
25:28.370 --> 25:30.420
over marching north versus south,

457
25:30.440 --> 25:32.170
unfolded from start to finish.

458
25:33.040 --> 25:34.300
The Central Committee

459
25:34.610 --> 25:36.130
tried many ways

460
25:36.440 --> 25:37.810
to win Zhang Guotao over

461
25:37.960 --> 25:40.240
and made plenty of concessions.

462
25:40.410 --> 25:42.720
But in the end, we couldn't hold him back.

463
25:43.000 --> 25:45.000
Right before this meeting started,

464
25:45.000 --> 25:47.480
we received another telegram from him.

465
25:47.720 --> 25:49.610
Not only did he refuse to go north,

466
25:49.680 --> 25:51.090
but he also had the nerve to falsely accuse us,

467
25:51.090 --> 25:53.200
claiming we were the ones splitting from him.

468
25:53.200 --> 25:56.760
He even said marching north is a dead end.

469
25:57.370 --> 26:01.040
It's absolutely outrageous!

470
26:01.480 --> 26:02.240
Exactly!

471
26:02.610 --> 26:04.680
He even sent telegrams to me, Fuchun,

472
26:04.760 --> 26:05.930
Lin Biao, and Nie Rongzhen

473
26:05.930 --> 26:07.410
individually,

474
26:07.680 --> 26:11.370
demanding we follow Xu and Chen down south.

475
26:11.520 --> 26:12.570
Like hell we'd listen to him!

476
26:12.570 --> 26:13.370
Yeah!

477
26:13.810 --> 26:14.610
I propose

478
26:14.810 --> 26:16.760
a fully public criticism

479
26:16.850 --> 26:18.680
of Zhang Guotao's erroneous path.

480
26:18.680 --> 26:20.410
He should be expelled from the Party!

481
26:20.410 --> 26:20.930
I agree!

482
26:21.040 --> 26:21.760
I agree!

483
26:22.090 --> 26:22.980
I agree too!

484
26:23.680 --> 26:26.610
Comrade Zedong, what are your thoughts?

485
26:29.370 --> 26:30.170
Comrades,

486
26:31.700 --> 26:32.700
I think

487
26:33.340 --> 26:36.100
it is not yet the time for us

488
26:36.530 --> 26:37.730
to issue Zhang Guotao

489
26:37.940 --> 26:39.770
an ultimatum.

490
26:41.680 --> 26:42.650
On the surface,

491
26:43.280 --> 26:46.130
it seems we've parted ways with the 4th Front Army.

492
26:46.280 --> 26:47.610
But you all must realize

493
26:47.890 --> 26:49.680
that many comrades in the 4th Front Army

494
26:49.680 --> 26:52.000
were actually deceived by Zhang Guotao.

495
26:52.330 --> 26:54.520
They don't know the whole truth.

496
26:54.550 --> 26:56.850
Many of them still hold the Central Committee

497
26:56.850 --> 26:59.170
in high regard and respect.

498
26:59.440 --> 27:00.850
That includes Comrade Xiangqian,

499
27:00.850 --> 27:02.580
as well as Comrade Li Xiannian.

500
27:03.200 --> 27:04.280
In fact, the cigarette I'm smoking right now

501
27:04.280 --> 27:05.850
was given to me by Comrade Li Xiannian.

502
27:05.850 --> 27:07.520
It was captured at the Baozuo battlefield

503
27:07.520 --> 27:09.040
and sent specially to me.

504
27:09.520 --> 27:10.320
The other day,

505
27:10.400 --> 27:13.000
I saw Comrade Xiaoping wearing a leather coat.

506
27:13.200 --> 27:15.960
He said his classmate from Moscow University,

507
27:15.960 --> 27:17.440
Fu Zhong, gave it to him.

508
27:17.760 --> 27:19.520
This isn't just about a cigarette

509
27:19.520 --> 27:21.000
or a leather coat.

510
27:21.290 --> 27:22.760
It shows the basic attitude

511
27:22.760 --> 27:25.090
of the 4th Front Army's cadres towards us.

512
27:26.280 --> 27:28.170
And Chen Changhao

513
27:28.410 --> 27:29.480
and Zhang Qinqiu

514
27:29.650 --> 27:31.240
were your classmates

515
27:31.330 --> 27:34.040
at Moscow Sun Yat-sen University.

516
27:34.170 --> 27:36.230
They all studied Marxism-Leninism.

517
27:36.650 --> 27:37.680
So tell me,

518
27:37.930 --> 27:40.170
can we really be separated

519
27:40.650 --> 27:42.850
from the comrades of the 4th Front Army?

520
27:44.370 --> 27:44.890
Exactly!

521
27:44.890 --> 27:46.170
Absolutely not.

522
27:46.440 --> 27:47.440
On the contrary,

523
27:47.760 --> 27:50.890
I think we should figure out a way

524
27:50.930 --> 27:54.120
to distinguish them from Zhang Guotao politically.

525
27:54.330 --> 27:55.730
Agreed. Agreed. Agreed.

526
27:55.890 --> 27:58.520
Now that the two front armies are separated,

527
27:58.650 --> 28:01.440
even if we want to unite and win them over,

528
28:01.470 --> 28:03.080
we can't even see them.

529
28:03.310 --> 28:04.720
Let's not forget,

530
28:05.090 --> 28:06.650
Comrades Zhu De, Bocheng,

531
28:06.760 --> 28:08.000
and the vast number of commanders and fighters

532
28:08.000 --> 28:09.370
of the 5th and 32nd Armies

533
28:09.370 --> 28:10.760
are all still with

534
28:11.040 --> 28:12.840
Zhang Guotao's Left Route Army.

535
28:12.890 --> 28:15.410
I believe they are loyal to the Central Committee.

536
28:15.410 --> 28:17.610
And I believe they will certainly help the Central Committee

537
28:17.610 --> 28:19.170
to explain, win over,

538
28:19.280 --> 28:20.650
and unite everyone.

539
28:20.760 --> 28:22.330
But if we now

540
28:22.480 --> 28:25.580
openly engage in a line struggle with Zhang Guotao,

541
28:26.480 --> 28:28.650
it will be hard for everyone to face each other later.

542
28:28.650 --> 28:30.130
Therefore, I suggest

543
28:30.410 --> 28:31.440
we temporarily

544
28:31.750 --> 28:33.130
keep the struggle against Zhang Guotao

545
28:33.130 --> 28:35.890
to the absolute minimum.

546
28:36.760 --> 28:39.090
We shouldn't convey it to the grassroots for now.

547
28:39.090 --> 28:41.950
Organizational resolutions can wait until later.

548
28:42.720 --> 28:43.440
Good.

549
28:43.930 --> 28:44.720
I agree.

550
28:45.170 --> 28:48.370
As long as we still see them as comrades,

551
28:48.890 --> 28:49.850
then as a family,

552
28:51.040 --> 28:53.610
we'll always have a chance to sit together again.

553
28:53.610 --> 28:54.070
Agreed.

554
28:54.090 --> 28:54.570
Agreed.

555
28:54.590 --> 28:55.250
Agreed.

556
29:01.990 --> 29:04.390
Many comrades might be

557
29:04.420 --> 29:06.240
thinking about another question in their hearts.

558
29:06.240 --> 29:07.280
Now that we

559
29:07.600 --> 29:10.440
only have these few troops left,

560
29:10.690 --> 29:13.330
should we still continue heading north?

561
29:23.200 --> 29:23.960
Yes.

562
29:24.760 --> 29:25.820
We must head north.

563
29:26.410 --> 29:28.140
We must resolutely head north!

564
29:31.130 --> 29:32.680
Our strength has been weakened,

565
29:32.680 --> 29:34.810
and our original strategic plan

566
29:34.810 --> 29:36.280
to establish revolutionary base areas

567
29:36.280 --> 29:38.520
in the Sichuan-Shaanxi-Gansu region must be adjusted.

568
29:38.520 --> 29:39.480
Right now,

569
29:39.650 --> 29:41.890
we should use guerrilla warfare

570
29:42.040 --> 29:43.650
to open up international connections.

571
29:43.650 --> 29:44.440
First,

572
29:44.650 --> 29:46.130
we need to establish new base areas

573
29:46.130 --> 29:47.680
in places close to the Soviet Union

574
29:47.680 --> 29:49.280
to expand our Red Army ranks.

575
29:49.520 --> 29:52.240
But no matter how our specific plans change,

576
29:52.370 --> 29:55.090
our overall strategic policy of heading north to resist Japanese aggression

577
29:55.090 --> 29:56.090
must never change.

578
29:56.090 --> 29:57.720
Good. Good.

579
29:58.020 --> 30:01.320
The Workers' and Peasants' Red Army led by the CPC

580
30:01.930 --> 30:05.540
must go to the forefront of the anti-Japanese war!

581
30:05.570 --> 30:06.930
Hear, hear.

582
30:17.680 --> 30:18.880
The E'jie Conference

583
30:19.220 --> 30:20.520
passed the "Decision of the Central Committee

584
30:20.520 --> 30:23.960
of the CPC on the Mistakes of Comrade Zhang Guotao,"

585
30:24.440 --> 30:27.720
proposing that all specific measures must be taken

586
30:27.890 --> 30:29.950
to correct Zhang Guotao's mistakes.

587
30:30.680 --> 30:32.740
To educate and win over Zhang Guotao,

588
30:33.220 --> 30:36.680
this decision was only conveyed to the Central Committee members

589
30:36.680 --> 30:38.940
and was not announced to the whole Party.

590
30:39.520 --> 30:41.130
The conference agreed with Peng Dehuai's

591
30:41.130 --> 30:43.370
proposal to downsize the troop organization

592
30:43.370 --> 30:45.570
to facilitate combat command.

593
30:45.680 --> 30:47.520
It decided to reorganize the 1st Red Army,

594
30:47.520 --> 30:50.130
the 3rd Red Army, and the Military Commission Column into

595
30:50.130 --> 30:54.180
the Shaanxi-Gansu Detachment of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army.

596
30:54.180 --> 30:56.240
Peng Dehuai was appointed Commander,

597
30:56.240 --> 30:58.200
Lin Biao as Deputy Commander,

598
30:58.390 --> 31:00.460
Mao Zedong as Political Commissar,

599
31:00.730 --> 31:02.570
Ye Jianying as Chief of Staff,

600
31:03.340 --> 31:05.510
Zhang Yunyi as Deputy Chief of Staff,

601
31:06.440 --> 31:09.480
Wang Jiaxiang as Director of the Political Department,

602
31:09.480 --> 31:11.610
and Yang Shangkun as Deputy Director.

603
31:11.970 --> 31:14.210
Mao Zedong and Zhou Enlai

604
31:14.330 --> 31:17.570
along with Peng Dehuai, Lin Biao, and Wang Jiaxiang

605
31:17.680 --> 31:20.730
formed a five-man military command group.

606
31:21.130 --> 31:23.150
Li De and Ye Jianying

607
31:23.440 --> 31:26.320
would join Deng Fa, Cai Shufan, and Li Weihan

608
31:26.610 --> 31:28.470
on the reorganization committee

609
31:28.500 --> 31:30.960
to oversee the restructuring of our forces.

610
31:36.580 --> 31:38.640
Let's all head back and get some rest.

611
31:38.810 --> 31:41.000
We're all exhausted, so let's turn in early.

612
31:41.000 --> 31:41.930
Get some sleep.

613
31:46.890 --> 31:51.000
Today is the 15th of the 8th lunar month, isn't it?

614
31:51.090 --> 31:51.890
That's right.

615
31:53.850 --> 31:54.720
That means

616
31:55.480 --> 31:58.130
this is our very first Mid-Autumn Festival

617
31:58.280 --> 31:59.810
since the Long March began.

618
32:01.650 --> 32:03.050
The Mid-Autumn Festival

619
32:04.090 --> 32:07.370
is supposed to be a time for reunion.

620
32:07.930 --> 32:09.570
I wonder when

621
32:09.890 --> 32:12.620
we'll finally get to see Commander-in-Chief Zhu

622
32:13.330 --> 32:16.040
and Comrade Liu Bocheng again.

623
32:22.370 --> 32:24.100
Let's not get too sentimental.

624
32:28.170 --> 32:30.570
Didn't we all come from every corner of the country

625
32:30.570 --> 32:32.850
and gather here together

626
32:32.880 --> 32:34.740
for our shared communist ideals?

627
32:35.240 --> 32:36.930
As long as our hearts are connected,

628
32:36.930 --> 32:39.090
across thousands of mountains and rivers,

629
32:39.090 --> 32:41.760
we will eventually reunite.

630
32:47.200 --> 32:48.650
A bosom friend afar

631
32:49.410 --> 32:50.940
brings a distant land near.

632
32:51.810 --> 32:53.810
May we all be blessed with longevity

633
32:54.520 --> 32:56.680
and share the beauty of this graceful moon, even miles apart.

634
32:56.680 --> 32:58.680
May we all be blessed with longevity

635
32:58.780 --> 33:01.750
and share the beauty of this graceful moon, even miles apart.

636
33:01.750 --> 33:04.370
These famous lines by the renowned Song poet Su Shi

637
33:04.370 --> 33:06.900
expressing his longing for his brother Su Zhe

638
33:07.200 --> 33:08.440
perfectly capture the current mood

639
33:08.440 --> 33:10.360
of the central leadership.

640
33:11.150 --> 33:12.350
At this very moment

641
33:12.700 --> 33:14.500
under the exact same moonlight,

642
33:14.850 --> 33:17.270
Red Army units stationed across different regions

643
33:17.270 --> 33:18.790
are also spending

644
33:18.860 --> 33:20.520
their own Mid-Autumn night.

645
33:21.130 --> 33:22.780
After trekking thousands of miles

646
33:22.780 --> 33:24.850
and marching towards Yanchuan County in northern Shaanxi,

647
33:24.850 --> 33:26.130
the 25th Red Army

648
33:26.330 --> 33:28.760
is about to join forces with the Northern Shaanxi Red Army.

649
33:28.760 --> 33:30.200
Their Mid-Autumn night

650
33:30.330 --> 33:32.280
is filled with immense joy.

651
33:32.570 --> 33:35.440
Such a melodious and lingering tune!

652
33:35.060 --> 33:37.710
[Cheng Zihua, Political Commissar of the 25th Red Army]

653
33:35.440 --> 33:37.160
You really sang out the vibrant spirit

654
33:37.160 --> 33:39.470
and boundless energy of our 25th Army!

655
33:39.810 --> 33:41.720
Let's keep the party going, comrades!

656
33:41.720 --> 33:43.890
Yeah!

657
33:44.170 --> 33:45.040
All right!

658
33:45.070 --> 33:45.870
Commander,

659
33:46.090 --> 33:48.520
why don't you sing a Peking Opera excerpt for us?

660
33:48.520 --> 33:49.680
What do you say, everyone?

661
33:49.680 --> 33:52.670
Yes!

662
33:52.830 --> 33:57.650
Give us a song! Give us a song!

663
33:57.940 --> 33:58.660
Come on.

664
34:01.810 --> 34:04.240
Tell me, what do you want to hear?

665
34:02.720 --> 34:04.010
[Xu Haidong, Commander of the 25th Red Army]

666
34:04.370 --> 34:05.720
Just sing your best piece

667
34:05.720 --> 34:07.520
the Gao School's "Execution at the Outer Gate".

668
34:07.520 --> 34:09.690
Great!

669
34:10.960 --> 34:12.929
I'll skip "Execution at the Outer Gate" today.

670
34:12.929 --> 34:16.219
Since it's the Mid-Autumn Festival and we're missing old friends,

671
34:16.219 --> 34:17.159
I'll perform a section of

672
34:17.159 --> 34:19.560
Commissar Wu's favorite, "The Three Great Sages".

673
34:19.560 --> 34:22.330
Bravo!

674
34:26.550 --> 34:41.190
There used to be a Three Great Sages

675
34:41.210 --> 34:46.290
Okay

676
34:47.290 --> 34:53.960
I heard people shouting in my ears

677
34:54.420 --> 35:00.300
[Cai Yang's men came to the side of the ancient city]

678
35:00.820 --> 35:05.220
The city tower helps you with three drums

679
35:05.370 --> 35:08.980
♪With the flags on all sides♪

680
35:09.000 --> 35:12.270
♪My head is beating♪

681
35:12.460 --> 35:14.630
Mr. Guan carried a knife across the sculpture

682
35:14.650 --> 35:17.460
♪It's just a round of drums♪

683
35:17.530 --> 35:20.180
Man is energetic Ma Youhuan

684
35:20.210 --> 35:22.870
♪It's just three drums♪

685
35:23.040 --> 35:25.930
Cai Yang's head is in front of the horse

686
35:31.280 --> 35:32.630
Gao Zhugen, you...

687
35:32.890 --> 35:34.110
When we camped out the day before yesterday,

688
35:34.110 --> 35:35.730
we heard the locals reciting a rhyme.

689
35:35.730 --> 35:38.810
"The Mid-Autumn moon is round and bright.

690
35:38.900 --> 35:41.670
The Matchmaker God descends tonight.

691
35:41.570 --> 35:43.510
[Han Xianchu, Company Commander, 1st Battalion, 225th Regiment, 25th Red Army]

692
35:41.920 --> 35:45.990
The red thread tied to lovers,

693
35:46.080 --> 35:50.410
for husband and wife to share a life ahead."

694
35:50.410 --> 35:52.080
Who taught you all that?

695
35:56.410 --> 35:59.040
That was great!

696
35:56.550 --> 35:58.930
[Zhou Shaolan, Nurse at the 25th Red Army Hospital]

697
36:00.700 --> 36:02.250
May we all be blessed with longevity

698
36:00.830 --> 36:04.770
[Shimen County, Hunan Province]

699
36:02.590 --> 36:05.480
and share the beauty of this graceful moon, even miles apart.

700
36:05.480 --> 36:08.010
In stark contrast to the joyous 25th Red Army,

701
36:08.560 --> 36:10.560
the 2nd and 6th Red Army Corps

702
36:10.560 --> 36:12.040
in the Hunan-Hubei-Sichuan-Guizhou Soviet Area

703
36:12.040 --> 36:13.640
were facing an Encirclement Campaign

704
36:13.640 --> 36:15.890
by over 130 Kuomintang regiments.

705
36:15.930 --> 36:18.520
Forced to retreat from Jinshi and Lizhou,

706
36:18.640 --> 36:20.960
they were now regrouping northwest

707
36:20.960 --> 36:22.480
of Shimen County in Changde.

708
36:22.480 --> 36:24.850
Their room to maneuver was shrinking rapidly,

709
36:24.850 --> 36:27.330
and the situation was becoming increasingly critical.

710
36:27.330 --> 36:29.190
This year's Mid-Autumn Festival

711
36:29.190 --> 36:31.750
was spent locked in a standoff with the enemy.

712
36:33.360 --> 36:34.780
Under the same moon,

713
36:35.480 --> 36:38.000
down in the Dayu Ridge region on the Jiangxi-Guangdong border,

714
36:38.000 --> 36:40.080
the Red Army guerrillas holding the line

715
36:40.080 --> 36:42.690
had been battered by the Nationalist army's relentless purges,

716
36:42.690 --> 36:44.600
suffering catastrophic losses.

717
36:44.960 --> 36:47.160
Survival was getting harder every day,

718
36:47.880 --> 36:51.280
and continuing the fight seemed almost impossible.

719
36:51.770 --> 36:56.020
[Dayu Ridge, Jiangxi-Guangdong Border]

720
36:55.130 --> 36:55.960
Tie him up.

721
36:57.740 --> 36:59.160
When the troops are marching,

722
36:59.160 --> 37:00.720
the thing I dread most is a fork in the road.

723
37:00.720 --> 37:02.030
Whenever we hit one,

724
37:02.160 --> 37:03.870
someone always slips away down the other path.

725
37:03.510 --> 37:06.380
[Chen Yi, Director of the Central Government Office, Chinese Soviet Republic]

726
37:03.970 --> 37:05.100
When we make camp,

727
37:05.400 --> 37:06.690
if it's a lone sentry,

728
37:06.790 --> 37:08.340
by morning, the man's gone.

729
37:08.480 --> 37:09.710
If we post a double watch,

730
37:09.710 --> 37:11.440
both of them take off together.

731
37:12.330 --> 37:13.270
Sometimes we'd post three guards,

732
37:13.270 --> 37:14.800
and all three would be gone.

733
37:14.970 --> 37:15.980
If this keeps up,

734
37:16.130 --> 37:17.110
the unit is going to fall apart.

735
37:17.110 --> 37:18.310
The water's boiling.

736
37:18.370 --> 37:19.020
Knife.

737
37:38.990 --> 37:40.280
Squeeze out the pus.

738
37:48.480 --> 37:49.330
Great.

739
37:49.820 --> 37:50.970
Now this wound

740
37:51.410 --> 37:53.340
won't be trying to kill me anymore.

741
37:53.640 --> 37:54.560
One more time.

742
37:54.930 --> 37:55.850
Knife.

743
38:13.890 --> 38:14.940
Quick, quick.

744
38:40.730 --> 38:41.690
Comrades,

745
38:42.700 --> 38:43.830
pass the word along.

746
38:44.120 --> 38:46.890
Anyone who wants to stay and fight for the revolution

747
38:46.890 --> 38:47.850
is welcome.

748
38:49.420 --> 38:51.620
But if you really can't hold on anymore,

749
38:52.180 --> 38:53.490
you can go home.

750
38:53.990 --> 38:56.690
Just leave the guns behind.

751
38:57.830 --> 38:59.630
To the comrades who are leaving,

752
39:01.300 --> 39:02.960
do not betray the revolution.

753
39:03.370 --> 39:04.970
Do not sell out our comrades,

754
39:05.530 --> 39:07.790
and absolutely do not stab us in the back.

755
39:08.210 --> 39:09.270
If you decide to go,

756
39:09.640 --> 39:10.950
on your way out,

757
39:11.260 --> 39:13.010
I can shake your hand.

758
39:13.760 --> 39:15.240
And if one day,

759
39:15.540 --> 39:17.340
you decide you want to come back,

760
39:17.410 --> 39:18.440
I hope

761
39:18.750 --> 39:20.350
I can shake your hand again,

762
39:21.200 --> 39:23.360
and call you "comrade".

763
39:24.000 --> 39:25.550
After the Nanchang Uprising,

764
39:25.550 --> 39:27.100
the army went through hell and high water.

765
39:27.100 --> 39:28.410
Among the officers at the regimental level and above,

766
39:28.410 --> 39:31.370
only Zhu De, Wang Erzhuo, and I were left.

767
39:31.660 --> 39:32.790
Just the three of us.

768
39:32.810 --> 39:34.880
But we didn't give up.

769
39:36.040 --> 39:38.840
We still managed to carve out a name for ourselves.

770
39:39.410 --> 39:40.620
Even if in the end,

771
39:40.640 --> 39:42.720
I'm the only one left standing,

772
39:43.040 --> 39:45.640
I'll still choose to fight for the revolution to the bitter end.

773
39:45.640 --> 39:46.730
Director Chen,

774
39:46.820 --> 39:48.270
if you can hold out,

775
39:48.360 --> 39:49.960
why couldn't we?

776
39:50.160 --> 39:51.160
We're not leaving!

777
39:51.160 --> 39:55.640
We're not leaving!

778
40:14.840 --> 40:15.880
Look, everyone.

779
40:16.920 --> 40:18.440
The moon is rising.

780
40:21.220 --> 40:24.620
The near mountain makes the distant moon seem small,

781
40:24.800 --> 40:28.160
so men claim the mountain is larger than the moon.

782
40:28.210 --> 40:31.530
If one had eyes as vast as the sky,

783
40:31.870 --> 40:35.460
they would see the mountain is tall, but the moon is boundless.

784
40:36.690 --> 40:37.730
Comrades!

785
40:38.370 --> 40:41.850
Revolutionaries need to have spirit.

786
40:41.850 --> 40:42.640
Am I right?

787
40:42.640 --> 40:43.930
Right!

788
40:44.560 --> 40:45.160
Let's go.

789
40:45.290 --> 40:46.850
Move out!

790
40:50.090 --> 40:52.090
May we all be blessed with longevity

791
40:52.370 --> 40:54.800
and share the beauty of this graceful moon, even miles apart.

792
40:54.800 --> 40:56.200
At this very moment,

793
40:56.470 --> 40:58.640
after the Central Red Army had marched north,

794
40:58.640 --> 41:00.890
the commanders and fighters of the 4th Front Army

795
41:00.890 --> 41:02.770
still in the Panzhou area

796
41:03.310 --> 41:06.060
were in a very different and complicated state of mind.

797
41:06.060 --> 41:07.390
My heart just feels like

798
41:07.770 --> 41:10.040
it's being weighed down by a massive boulder.

799
41:10.040 --> 41:13.480
When we joined forces at Maogong,

800
41:14.000 --> 41:16.600
our 4th Front Army and the 1st Front Army

801
41:16.770 --> 41:17.850
were really like

802
41:17.960 --> 41:20.760
family members reuniting after a lifetime apart.

803
41:20.770 --> 41:22.930
Singing and dancing...

804
41:23.080 --> 41:25.730
what a lively scene that was.

805
41:26.560 --> 41:28.640
Just look at the battle we won at Baozuo a couple days ago.

806
41:28.410 --> 41:29.940
[Li Xiannian, Political Commissar of the 30th Red Army]

807
41:28.810 --> 41:29.890
Cheng Shicai and I

808
41:29.890 --> 41:31.690
dug through the loot

809
41:31.910 --> 41:33.810
to find the best beef, biscuits, and canned food

810
41:33.810 --> 41:36.040
and sent them over to the central leadership.

811
41:36.040 --> 41:38.400
Comrade Bo Gu couldn't stop thanking us.

812
41:38.890 --> 41:40.070
I even brought Chairman Mao

813
41:40.070 --> 41:41.490
a couple cartons of cigarettes,

814
41:41.490 --> 41:43.290
and he was absolutely thrilled!

815
41:45.480 --> 41:47.930
It also reminds me of early July,

816
41:48.640 --> 41:51.600
when I was at the Weigu River.

817
41:52.120 --> 41:54.560
I was so desperate to see Comrade Peng Dehuai

818
41:54.560 --> 41:56.690
that I crossed two massive mountains.

819
41:57.690 --> 42:00.520
When I finally reached the river,

820
42:02.560 --> 42:04.730
it was just way too wide.

821
42:04.860 --> 42:07.180
The only iron chain bridge across

822
42:07.410 --> 42:09.210
had been destroyed by the enemy.

823
42:09.370 --> 42:11.120
The current was incredibly fast

824
42:11.120 --> 42:12.380
and roaring so loudly.

825
42:12.560 --> 42:15.210
Comrade Peng Dehuai took off his bamboo hat

826
42:15.330 --> 42:16.210
right then and there

827
42:16.210 --> 42:17.290
and gestured at me

828
42:17.390 --> 42:18.720
just like this.

829
42:18.930 --> 42:19.880
Then he shouted at me,

830
42:19.880 --> 42:23.050
"Xiangqian! Xiangqian!"

831
42:23.850 --> 42:24.650
I yelled back,

832
42:24.750 --> 42:25.900
"Yes! What?"

833
42:26.960 --> 42:28.600
He replied, "You go forward!

834
42:30.040 --> 42:31.270
Forward!"

835
42:31.690 --> 42:34.400
So the two of us walked along the river

836
42:34.770 --> 42:36.160
for who knows how long,

837
42:36.960 --> 42:38.850
until we spotted a zipline.

838
42:38.960 --> 42:42.480
Hanging from it was a broken basket

839
42:42.520 --> 42:44.180
woven out of willow branches.

840
42:44.840 --> 42:46.590
I jumped right into it!

841
42:46.730 --> 42:49.160
The soldiers tried to stop me,

842
42:49.210 --> 42:50.440
warning me it wasn't safe.

843
42:50.440 --> 42:52.070
But I couldn't care less about that!

844
42:52.070 --> 42:54.110
I just kicked off the rock,

845
42:54.560 --> 42:56.520
and swoosh, I slid right across.

846
42:56.560 --> 42:59.440
Comrade Peng Dehuai was worried I'd fall,

847
42:59.600 --> 43:01.780
so he stood on the opposite bank like this,

848
43:01.780 --> 43:02.960
ready to catch me.
